  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Reading this view",
      "items": [
        "snake_case labels are real session.phase strings. Nodes in the 'conceptual step' legend group, or with tag 'conceptual'/'phase group', are not phase strings.",
        "Pilot calls move a phase only after telemetry confirms the claim (_at_hold, _at_crossing, _lined_up). Take-off, landing and vacating come from the mission track alone (airfield.py 44-50)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "One movement lane per airfield",
      "items": [
        "One lane covers every runway: line-up, take-off, crossing and landing. Order is emergency first, then arrivals, then departures, then call order (airfield.py 945-947).",
        "A grant goes to the first eligible session, and only while no controlled aircraft occupies any runway, with tower service on the session's channel (1060-1076, 1086-1098).",
        "A clearance with no readback after 60 model seconds lapses and is marked expired. It is not reissued until the pilot asks again (101, 1030-1036)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Other departure views",
      "items": [
        "Runway crossing and return to parking",
        "Clearance revocations, aborts and stale bridge",
        "Early closure and uncleared take-off",
        "Session safeguards (death, respawn, epoch, transfer)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Transition evidence (file lines)",
      "items": [
        "telemetry: on ground here: telemetry: ground_airfield_id matches (881-885)",
        "pilot: request taxi: pilot call, ground required (1588-1591)",
        "exact readback: exact runway (1709-1718, 477-518)",
        "pilot call + at hold: pilot call + _at_hold geometry (1739-1742)",
        "lane granted: scheduler: free lane, clear runway, tower (1060-1071)",
        "exact readback: jumps to lined_up if already aligned (1717-1721)",
        "telemetry: aligned: telemetry 888-890, or pilot call confirmed (1748-1752)",
        "takeoff granted: lane holder only, runway clear (1053-1059)",
        "exact readback: 1717",
        "telemetry: takeoff: in_air or takeoff event (879-880, 906-915)",
        "10 nm or pilot switching: telemetry HANDOFF_NM (891-892), pilot handoff (1820-1824)",
        "readback_problem checks the exact runway, the clearance term and conflicting words (airfield.py 477-518)."
      ]
    }
  ]
